      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10820071::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC10820071::web::017::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A short post-deposition anneal can promote controlled oxidation in the coating.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed HVOF and annealing treatment can selectively enrich Al at FCC/BCC interfaces.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed processing route can increase FCC/BCC interface density.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Creep resistance is primarily governed by solute-enriched, lattice-distorted FCC/BCC interfaces.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solute-enriched, lattice-distorted FCC/BCC interfaces act as dislocation locks.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::008::in_situ_tem_straining_tests"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "During continuous high-temperature stress, dislocations nucleate and propagate through slip bands.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial dislocation locking retards dislocation climb.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial dislocation locking inhibits slip transmission across phase boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::008::in_situ_tem_straining_tests"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Suppressing dislocation motion at the engineered interfaces hinders strain-localizing shear-band formation and reduces creep strain.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::008::in_situ_tem_straining_tests"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, the engineered coating will have a lower creep strain rate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, the engineered coating will show less propagation of slip and shear bands.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the baseline, the engineered coating will retain more microhardness during sustained loading.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocation pile-ups will be observable at solute-enriched FCC/BCC interfaces.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mechanism is expected to remain effective at approximately 400–600 MPa and 800 °C for durations up to 1000 hours.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain a statistically significant reduction exceeding about 20% in creep strain rate, together with diminished slip or shear bands and demonstrable interfacial dislocation locking, would refute the proposed mechanism.",
